A||||7||Greg Piet||Harmonic Balancer installation||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||01-07-2000||05:02 PM||||OK I know the balancer is keyed, but i cant get the darn thing on.  I do not have special tool j29113 as listed in the pontiac manual, but i have been using the good old rubber mallet, and oils/lubricants, but no luck.  I was thinking of getting a longer bolt to press it in, but of course the auto parts store doesnt have one.  What did others do?||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||01-07-2000||10:30 PM||||I just did this a month ago, and I remember cussing some engineer out for the bolt being too short.  I found a thin piece of metal (leftover deadbolt striker plate, believe it or not) in my garage and used it like a flat washer.  The stock flat washer is about a sixteenth of an inch too thick to work.  A fender washer might work if you can find one with a big enough i.d.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||01-08-2000||03:19 AM||||Well after going to a number of GM parts places and hardware stores to get a 12X1.5 metric bolt that was longer to no avail, and even more auto parts stores i found a harmonic balancer remover and installer kit at checker auto.  I went to 4 checkers parts stores, and the first three looked at me like I was on drugs, then fianlly the fourth store said "yeah we got those".  GRRRRR  that just gets me all angry.  <P>Oh well at least that problem is remedied.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||01-09-2000||12:51 AM||||Glad to hear you got it done.<P>How much did the remover/installer cost you?  I bought a puller for $15 at Advance Auto, but it didn't even come with the right size bolts, so I had to use the crank pulley bolts with it.  No big deal.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||01-09-2000||02:45 AM||||My crank pulley bolt wasnt long enough even with a thinner washer.  The puller and installer cost me 60 bucks, and i can return it for 55 bucks.   So it will cost me 5 bucks to rent it.  I started installing the pulley and it was a tight fit.  I ran out of Daylight, so i have to finish it tomorrow.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||01-09-2000||09:18 PM||||Just as a warning to others.  After i put the balancer on, i went to install the pulley.  The threads for the 4 bolts were different so i had to get differnet bolts.  So be careful not to mess up the threads on the new balancer thinking the old bolts will work fine||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||01-09-2000||11:23 PM||||??????<P>What kind of balancer did you get?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||01-09-2000||11:38 PM||||I got the balancer from checker auto.<BR>The box says it is made by Pioneer Inc part number DA-1733 ||||reg||1
